# VGC Core — native client-rects farbling (getBoundingClientRect / getClientRects)
# STATUS: ✅ VERIFIED — real, git-apply-able diff (built + validated on M151). UNION approach:
# getClientRects() farbles each rect (~±1e-4 px, deterministic per --vgc-seed); getBoundingClientRect()
# is built from the SAME per-rect farbling and then unioned, so union(getClientRects) == getBoundingClientRect
# EXACTLY (a detector comparing them finds no discrepancy) and a DETACHED element stays all-zero exactly
# like stock Chrome — no invariant is broken. The JS layer (stealth-extra.ts) SKIPS its own client-rects
# override whenever the VGC engine is present (signal __vgcScreenNative from screen.cc), NOT via a
# detached-element probe — a direct VgcNoiseRectF(bcr) that made detached non-zero would itself be a tell
# (stock detached bcr == 0) and could split bcr from union(getClientRects) on multi-line inline elements.
# Reuses --vgc-seed (already in kVgcSwitches, patch 02).
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/element.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/element.cc
